_No response_

review_comments:
> Not sure what is the correct fix, the empty chunk is not added into the chain so I assume will not be serialized either.

The expectation when calling `LinkPrefix / LinkSuffix` is that ownership (in terms of pooling) is passing to the receiver. In the case of a zero length `BlobBuilder` there is no ownership transfer, instead the value is dropped. That instead should be returned to the pool aka cleared and freed.

Yes this does produce a slight breaking change in that previously you used to be able to do the following: 

```csharp
var builder1 = new BlobBuilder();
var builder2 = new BlobBuilder();
builder1.LinkSuffix(builder2);
builder2.WriteBytes(0, 1); 
```

At the same time this only works when `blobBuilder2.Length == 0`, in all other cases it would throw. It would be very odd for a consumer to have this pattern at all because `LinkPrefix/LinkSuffix` normally results in the target being read only.
